        "Content": "Leonard Wilson Keenan \r\n\r\nOur business is you..\r\n\r\n3 bedroom, 3 Bathroom Semi Detached  Extended Family Home \r\nAttic Space currently used as 4th bedroom \r\n\r\nRichard Todd and Leonard Wilson Keenan are delighted to present 36 Woodland Park to the Co Dublin property market.\r\nNestled in the highly sought-after Woodland Park development, this beautifully extended three-bedroom, three-bathroom semi-detached family home offers spacious, light-filled accommodation perfectly suited to modern family living. Occupying a superb position overlooking a large green area within this quiet and mature residential development, the property combines generous living space with a wonderful coastal location just minutes from all the amenities that the vibrant town of Rush has to offer.\r\n\r\nOn arrival, you are welcomed by a well-maintained front garden and a private driveway providing valuable off-street parking. A gated side entrance offers convenient access to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nStepping inside, the bright and inviting entrance hallway immediately creates a warm first impression. Cleverly designed with family living in mind, the hallway features a guest WC tucked neatly beneath the stairs along with additional storage space.\r\n\r\nTo the front of the property, the elegant living room is flooded with natural light from the attractive bay window overlooking the front garden and green area. A feature fireplace incorporating a wood-burning stove creates a warm and cosy focal point, making this the perfect room to relax and unwind. French doors lead effortlessly through to the heart of the home, an impressive open-plan kitchen, dining and family room that has been thoughtfully extended to create an exceptional living space.\r\n\r\nThe contemporary kitchen has been finished to a high standard and offers an abundance of quality base and eye-level units together with generous worktop space, making it as practical as it is stylish. The extension is beautifully illuminated by Velux roof windows, creating a bright and airy atmosphere throughout. Beyond the dining area is an additional reception space currently used as a family room, offering superb flexibility for modern family life. Whether utilised as a children's playroom, home office, snug or second living area, this versatile room adapts effortlessly to a family's changing needs. Large sliding doors open directly onto the rear garden, creating an excellent indoor-outdoor flow and making the space ideal for entertaining family and friends throughout the year.\r\n\r\nThe rear garden has been carefully maintained and enjoys a paved patio area, providing the perfect setting for al fresco dining, summer barbecues or simply relaxing in peaceful surroundings.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the accommodation continues to impress with three generously proportioned bedrooms. Two spacious bedrooms are positioned to the front of the property, while the principal bedroom overlooks the rear garden and benefits from fitted wardrobes together with a private en-suite bathroom. A well-appointed family bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe attic has also been converted to provide valuable additional space. While currently used as a fourth bedroom by the present owners, it is designated as storage accommodation and features Velux windows that fill the room with natural light. This versatile space would also make an ideal home office, hobby room or children's den.\r\n\r\nWoodland Park is recognised as one of Rush's most desirable residential developments, offering a peaceful, family-friendly environment within walking distance of the town centre. Rush is a thriving coastal community renowned for its beautiful beaches, excellent schools and superb range of amenities. Residents can enjoy an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, shops and supermarkets, while families are particularly well catered for with a choice of highly regarded primary and secondary schools nearby.\r\n\r\nThe area also boasts an impressive range of sporting and recreational facilities, including GAA, soccer, cricket, sailing, tennis and golf clubs, together with numerous coastal walks and outdoor pursuits. Both the North Beach and South Beach are only a short distance from the property, offering miles of sandy shoreline to enjoy throughout the year.\r\n\r\nCommuters will appreciate the property's excellent connectivity. Rush & Lusk Train Station is approximately 4 kilometres away and provides regular rail services to Dublin City Centre, while frequent Dublin Bus services also serve the area. The M1 motorway, M50 and Dublin Airport are all within easy reach, making this an ideal location for those seeking the perfect balance between coastal living and convenient access to the city.\r\n\r\nCombining generous accommodation, a thoughtfully designed extension, a converted attic, beautifully maintained gardens and an enviable location overlooking a green open space, No. 36 Woodland Park represents an outstanding opportunity to acquire a superb family home in one of North County Dublin's most sought-after coastal towns.\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
